        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(shared): bound ignore-file reads during workspace scans",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`addIgnoreRules` in `src/shared/ignore-rules.ts` reads `.gitignore`, `.ignore`, and `.fdignore` files with `readFileSync(..., \"utf-8\")` and no size limit. A malicious or runaway ignore file in a scanned workspace can be loaded entirely into memory, causing the CLI or agent workspace scan to OOM before any rules are applied.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nIgnore files are line-oriented pattern lists; even large monorepos rarely exceed a few hundred KiB. Adding a 4 MiB byte cap lets legitimate ignore files pass through while preventing an unbounded read from exhausting process memory. The existing `catch` block means oversized files are skipped silently, matching the current graceful behavior for unreadable files.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Workspace scans (`openclaw agent`, skill loading, etc.) no longer buffer arbitrarily large ignore files.\n- Oversized `.gitignore` / `.ignore` / `.fdignore` files are skipped instead of crashing the process.\n- Normal-sized ignore files work exactly as before.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Replaced `readFileSync` with `readRegularFileSync({ filePath, maxBytes: IGNORE_FILE_MAX_BYTES })` in `src/shared/ignore-rules.ts`.\n- Added `src/shared/ignore-rules.test.ts` with regression tests covering normal ignore files, large-but-under-cap files, and files that exceed the cap.\n- Local test run:\n  ```\n  node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/shared/ignore-rules.test.ts --run\n  # 3 tests passed\n  ```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nI created `.gitignore` files at, above, and below the new 4 MiB cap, plus a symlinked `.gitignore` pointing to a regular file, and ran workspace scan ignore-rule loading:\n\n```text\n$ OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/shared/ignore-rules.test.ts --run\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.shared-core.config.ts\n RUN  v4.1.9\n ✓ |shared-core| src/shared/ignore-rules.test.ts (4 tests) 1447ms\n     ✓ silently skips an oversized ignore file instead of buffering it\n     ✓ follows a symlinked .gitignore to a regular file\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  4 passed (4)\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 12.85s\n```\n\n- A 2.4 MiB ignore file is still loaded normally.\n- A 13 MiB ignore file is silently skipped instead of buffering the whole file.\n- A symlinked `.gitignore` is resolved and its regular target is still honored, preserving the previous workspace-scan behavior.",
        "branch": "fix/bound-ignore-file-reads",
